1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,560
An off-the-shelf AI agent, planning on Kiln, was asked to buy a GPU hour from a cheaper seller that is not on the list. The vault on TRON refused, and recorded the stop on-chain.

2
00:00:11,462 --> 00:00:16,062
Kiln explains it in plain words, shown only because it repeats the audit's verdict.

3
00:00:16,963 --> 00:00:22,813
This is the vault's public event: SpendBlocked, with the receipt hash and the reason. Anyone can read it.

4
00:00:23,715 --> 00:00:32,625
This is Spendline, a wallet and policy layer for an AI purchasing agent. A person draws the line. The agent only asks. The vault decides.

5
00:00:33,527 --> 00:00:39,947
The person sets a budget, a per-payment cap, the sellers, and a deadline, one short step at a time.

6
00:00:40,848 --> 00:00:45,718
Then signs it with the owner key, on their own machine. STOP is signed the same way.

7
00:00:46,621 --> 00:00:51,821
The feed shows spending against the line, newest first: paid, or stopped with a reason.

8
00:00:52,723 --> 00:00:55,743
Over budget once the fee is added: stopped on-chain.

9
00:00:56,645 --> 00:01:01,925
The person can press STOP at any time. The next payment was stopped as PAUSED, on-chain.

10
00:01:02,826 --> 00:01:09,916
A short time window: one payment inside it, then the same request after it closed. Stopped: deadline passed.

11
00:01:10,818 --> 00:01:18,818
The audit, rebuilt from public records only: 34 receipts, 20 paid inside, 14 stopped, 0 problems.

12
00:01:19,721 --> 00:01:22,551
The same check from the command line, with no key.

13
00:01:23,453 --> 00:01:41,353
Any agent that speaks MCP can use Spendline as its wallet, even one we did not write; Kiln's own record still witnesses every payment. Here our host plans on Kiln: code priced three pay calls; two were paid, the unknown seller was stopped. Sent again, every call was refused on-chain as a repeat.

14
00:01:42,256 --> 00:01:53,466
And a second witness. In plain words: Kiln's own logbook and the blockchain tell the same story for every AI call on the organizer's account, and each call came 2 to 10 seconds before its payment.

15
00:01:54,368 --> 00:02:02,258
A teammate asks: was anything paid after I pressed STOP? Kiln picks the receipt. The verdict comes from the audit, never from the model.

16
00:02:03,160 --> 00:02:14,100
On Friday, one command writes the statement: paid by seller, refused attempts, an intent flag, and a CSV for the accountant. Tune shows what next week's line would have done.

17
00:02:15,002 --> 00:02:26,072
Efficiency: one LLM call per purchase. No-think cut median output from 223 to 36 tokens. Energy is an estimate: 180 watts times measured time.

18
00:02:26,975 --> 00:02:31,695
Spendline. Not an agent that can pay, but a payment that can prove it was allowed.
